bic_trace_step.reason:
In cc_mac_digest(), after cc_map_result() succeeds, if cc_map_hash_request_final() fails, the code only calls cc_unmap_req() and returns -ENOMEM, but does not call cc_unmap_result() to unmap the result buffer DMA mapping. This causes a DMA mapping leak. The relevant lines are: 
	if (cc_map_result(dev, state, digestsize)) { ... cc_unmap_req(dev, state, ctx); return -ENOMEM; } 
	if (cc_map_hash_request_final(...)) { dev_err(...); cc_unmap_req(dev, state, ctx); return -ENOMEM; } 
No cc_unmap_result is called in the second error path.
